# Prespecified bounded MCQ quality gate for Issue #23

No quality candidate outputs were consulted when selecting questions, inputs,
packing, answer parser or acceptance conditions. This package is CPU preparation
only; hardware collection belongs to root and has not been performed here.

The frozen plan digest is
`32b9464fb1f332263932db3b4e5a5278ee267a77d100f5ca0d6be4158b589282`.
The canonical benchmark checkout is `55181feb086af61c1cb953225ebe7e70167f77bb`.
Navigation followed its `DATA_INDEX.md`, generated collection index and
`reports/vllm-hust-midterm-20261019/README.md` to the existing aligned MMLU
archive and its original 200-ID selection. No historical result metrics are
substituted for fresh native/raw/group controls.

## Exact public task and gold provenance

The dataset is [MMLU-Pro at fixed revision b189ec7](https://huggingface.co/datasets/TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro/tree/b189ec765aa7ed75c8acfea42df31fdae71f97be).
The test/validation parquet SHA-256 values match the canonical adapter:
`0e24a191921c2f453518a537a8b2117bd137e7714d4ef1565e9ba06c1ecb9ad8` and
`139423c23722e480c807ac4a191409a710cfce4eba744c1d641cf88e730e2078`.
The selection-ID bytes have SHA-256
`798ca7c0c70b98eacc45800a8679cf2283c2ae2ceade5b778d77b60a9ad138fe`;
the unchanged 200 materialized prompts have SHA-256
`fb79b6fa98f232282a948e4a17f404f80c03dc2bae05af57b95b9cc0651b3506`.

For each selected ID, preparation looked up the actual public question row,
verified gold letter/index/options, then reconstructed the entire original
five-shot prompt from its five validation examples and target question.
Every reconstructed prompt matches the archived bytes exactly. The upstream
instruction was recovered from the existing prompt and its known original
digest verified before use. `gold-source-rows.jsonl` and per-case source-row
hashes retain the exact gold mapping. Questions and answers were not generated
or chosen after inspecting outputs. Existing source license/attribution remains
with the canonical adapter; these local raw question artifacts are not an
authorization to republish an unrelated corpus wholesale.

The fixed subset contains 200 questions across all 14 subjects. It uses real
ground-truth multiple-choice correctness, not output text equality, apparent
fluency or a model judging its own answers. It is a named subset, not the full
MMLU-Pro leaderboard protocol.

## Frozen inputs and admission

Canonical Hugging Face `AutoTokenizer.apply_chat_template` rendered the local
Qwen3.5 template with `enable_thinking=False`, `add_generation_prompt=True`;
encoding used `add_special_tokens=False`. Result: 280,865 prompt tokens total,
exactly the canonical historical total; individual lengths 918–2,495. The
tokenizer/template files and package versions are hashed/recorded in plan.json.
Preparation imported torch/torch_npu incidentally through this environment's
tokenizer dependencies, but called no device, tensor or model operation.
The initial Arrow import failed because of NumPy1/2 mismatch; that failed log
is retained. Successful preparation used the existing separate CPU Arrow
reader process and the existing inference tokenizer environment.

Packing preserves original selection order: 25 batches of eight cases, with
maximum total prompt tokens 15,931. Every prompt plus the 2,048 output-token cap
fits max-model-len 16,384. No prompt or output is silently shortened.

Each fresh runtime uses an actual `InprocClient`. For every batch, admit its
first case alone. Step the coordinator until that request has exactly one
output token; then enqueue the other seven frozen cases before the next step.
The trigger reads real scheduler state because `LLM.enqueue` uses FINAL_ONLY
client output. If the seed finishes at its first token, retain that fact and
release peers; that batch may fail the separate mixed-P/D coverage gate. No
case substitution, retry or HTTP timing decision is allowed. Fully drain each
batch before the next. Internal IDs bind to external IDs through real output
processor state, never string parsing. Returned prompt IDs are verified.

All arms use temperature 0, seed 42, max_tokens 2048, EOS enabled, ordinary
worker classes and no full-vocabulary numerical capture. The existing CoT
prompts require the original output budget; replacing it with 8 or 16 tokens
would change the quality task. Native controls retain standard chunked prefill;
raw/group MuxPD disable it by design. Other common runtime settings match.
Group-compatible `enable_npugraph_ex=False` and `enable_static_kernel=False`
are explicit in **all** three configurations, so this is a separately recorded
common compiler configuration rather than a claim about all compiler modes.

## Acceptance fixed before collection

Run two fresh native controls, raw MuxPD and grouped MuxPD, each on the same
200 cases and fixed packing. Ordinary native runtime sources, plugin source,
producer digest, interpreter/package versions and recorded worker environment
must match. Existing dirty trees are bound by exact git-diff bytes/digest and
modified/untracked file digests; unrelated changes are not reverted. Native
control launch settings must be identical; differences
between native and candidate are restricted to the declared scheduler/worker
and chunked-prefill selection. The supplied scorer rejects unmanifested or
differing dirty state rather than assuming a commit identifies executed bytes.

The deterministic answer parser is the copied, hashed canonical adapter's
three-stage A–J extraction, with no random guessing. Only an in-range letter
matching the public gold answer is correct. Missing requests, runtime/API
errors, invalid/out-of-range answers and output-cap truncations score wrong.
All 200 cases must finish without runtime error or truncation in both controls
and the candidate; a truncated final output fails completion even if it
contains an earlier parsable answer.

The quality veto is strict: **one candidate wrong answer on any case both
native controls answered correctly fails**. Improvements on other cases cannot
compensate. Candidate total correct must additionally be at least the lower
native control total. A vacuous empty both-native-correct set is rejected.

`bounded_answer_quality_gate_passed` applies only to these answer/completion
checks. `full_frozen_plan_passed` additionally requires a hashed actual
schedule/retirement receipt showing P layer progress and D token retirement in
the same transaction in **each of the 25 mixed batches**. This stricter coverage
interpretation is frozen here before device collection. It does not claim
physical simultaneous kernels. All uncovered batches are reported and cannot
be hidden by successful answer scores.

The report includes all four correctness transitions for candidate versus each
native control, native versus native, and grouped versus raw. It retains case
IDs, invalid extractions, incomplete cases, all answers and token IDs. Native
variability is disclosed; it does not relax the stable-correct veto after the
fact.

## Confidence and limited power

Report exact binomial 95% intervals for each accuracy and a conservative paired
difference interval obtained from simultaneous exact bounds on the two
discordant probabilities. Report a one-sided 95% upper bound on the candidate
new-error proportion among both-native-correct cases. Even zero new errors
among 200 such cases would only bound that proportion near 1.49% under the
binomial assumptions; the actual stable-correct denominator may be smaller.

This deterministic selected subset does not by itself supply random-sampling
coverage for all MMLU-Pro or arbitrary text. These intervals are descriptive
under their stated exchangeability assumptions. The exact McNemar p-value is
diagnostic only: nonsignificance cannot establish equivalence. Passing this
gate does not establish arbitrary-text semantic equivalence, token/logit
identity or eliminate rare numerical errors. Report the bounded result with
that limitation intact; retain the numerical diagnostics separately.

## CPU verification and root-owned execution

`run_quality.py dry-run` validates input hashes and launch arguments without
importing vLLM. `run_quality.py run` is the explicit device-owning action; this
agent has not invoked it. Root's controlled supervisor should copy the frozen
directory, scripts, execution identity manifest and engine arguments into each
attempt and preserve failure/cleanup receipts. Do not use these observed runs
as latency or throughput benchmarks.

```bash
python run_quality.py dry-run --frozen frozen --plan-sha256 32b9464fb1f332263932db3b4e5a5278ee267a77d100f5ca0d6be4158b589282 --role native --engine-args native-engine-args.json
python score_quality.py --frozen frozen --native1 /N1/run.json --native2 /N2/run.json --candidate /RAW/run.json --output /NEW/raw-quality.json
python score_quality.py --frozen frozen --native1 /N1/run.json --native2 /N2/run.json --candidate /GROUP/run.json --raw-reference /RAW/run.json --output /NEW/group-quality.json
```

Synthetic tests exercise the veto despite offsetting improvements, native
variability/floor, invalid/error/truncation scoring, frozen gold/token packing,
real receipt gating, provenance rejection, and FINAL_ONLY seed admission with
live and immediately finished seeds. These tests are not measured model data.
